WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.120
Teacher midterm practice, question 1.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:08.479
In Figure X, what are the Miller indices of plane A? Five choices are listed.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:15.014
Plane A passes through the origin itself, so one intercept would be zero.

4
00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:18.524
The fix is to move the origin to a neighboring corner.

5
00:00:18.524 --> 00:00:21.459
Take the front corner, one cell along x.

6
00:00:22.078 --> 00:00:25.848
From that corner, plane A meets z at three quarters, meets y at

7
00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:29.565
one half, and meets x one full cell back, at minus one.

8
00:00:30.185 --> 00:00:33.472
Take reciprocals: minus one, two, and four thirds.

9
00:00:34.092 --> 00:00:38.171
Multiply by three to clear the fraction: minus three, six, four.

10
00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:41.205
Write the negative index with a bar over it.

11
00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:43.429
Plane A is bar three, six, four.

12
00:00:45.029 --> 00:00:47.511
The answer is D: bar three, six, four.

13
00:00:48.332 --> 00:00:52.380
If a plane passes through the origin, move the origin first.

14
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.029
Otherwise you get a zero intercept and an infinite index.
